#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068395 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7229f1d0-4ba7-50ff-b5be-5697c886a175" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Compound Inequalities"}] :question/id #uuid "0901e241-519b-50ee-ab5f-50b2f631e948" :question/math-academy-id "e-13932" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $0 \\leq 3x+6 < 15$." :question/worked-solution "We isolate $x$ by applying the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 0 &\\leq 3x+6 < 15 \\\\[5pt] 0 - 6 &\\leq 3x + 6 -6 < 15-6 \\\\[5pt] -6 &\\leq 3x < 9 \\\\[5pt] \\dfrac{-6}{3} &\\leq \\dfrac{3x}{3} < \\dfrac{9}{3} \\\\[5pt] -2 &\\leq x < 3 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n-2 \\leq x < 3\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068396 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5930113e-6971-59c9-810a-97fd25bc4f89" :knowledge-point/title "Compound Inequalities That Require Flipping the Inequality Sign"}] :question/id #uuid "8208b5ba-8c54-5c05-a9f4-04aa30f8892f" :question/math-academy-id "e-13933" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $-1 < -2x + 1 \\leq 7$." :question/worked-solution "We isolate $x$ by applying the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & < - 2x + 1 \\le 7 \\\\ -1 - 1 & < - 2x + 1 - 1 \\le 7 - 1 \\\\ -2 & < - 2x \\le 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nAt this point, we need to divide by $-2$. However, because we are dividing by a negative, we also need to flip the inequality signs.\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & < - 2x \\le 6 \\\\ \\frac{-2}{-2} & >\\frac{-2x}{-2}\\ge\\frac{6}{-2} \\\\ 1 & > x \\ge - 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe solution can be written as\n\n$$\n1 > x \\geq - 3\n$$\n\nbut this is somewhat difficult to read because the larger number is on the left rather than the right. So, we will rewrite the solution by reversing the order of the numbers:\n\n$$\n-3 \\leq x < 1\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068397 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b3ff37f0-6e45-5da4-ac87-1b93c8df3e80" :knowledge-point/title "Representing Solutions of Compound Inequalities on Number Lines"}] :question/id #uuid "7f671658-055a-599d-8f1f-416570e604b6" :question/math-academy-id "e-13935" :question/problem "Represent the solution to the inequality $-3 < 1-2x < 11$ using a number line." :question/worked-solution "We isolate $x$ by applying the addition and multiplication principles, as usual.\n\nFirst, we apply the addition principle:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & < 1 - 2x < 11 \\\\ -3 - 1 & < 1 - 2x - 1 < 11 - 1 \\\\ -4 & < - 2x < 10\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide by $-2$. Note that since we are dividing by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality signs.\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & < - 2x < 10 \\\\ \\frac{-4}{-2} & > \\frac{-2x}{-2} > \\frac{10}{-2} \\\\ 2 & > x > - 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe solution can be written as $2 > x > -5$, but this is somewhat difficult to read because the larger number is on the left rather than the right. So, we will rewrite the solution by reversing the order of the numbers:\n\n$$\n-5 < x < 2\n$$\n\nWe can represent this solution using a number line, as follows.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/388/Source/Images/692aff95e86f691ddb4f9957282f51c5.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186251034 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b3ff37f0-6e45-5da4-ac87-1b93c8df3e80" :knowledge-point/title "Representing Solutions of Compound Inequalities on Number Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8bade343-2ece-57a5-b8df-d48c74b4b4e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944026/assets/120c8bbf904e4df194f0c4e614d5a1090ba0121ee7718571683c0c9ac9bb6b15.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251036} {:answer/id #uuid "98adbe9b-190f-5381-9ffe-f67b6cc11a0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944026/assets/f3d5c539ab5ce8d1820dc8627ddd981e6871ded73f10648bf02f8a03c3eb5185.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251037} {:answer/id #uuid "fba22c1f-6007-5b62-b056-ab9291f5830d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944026/assets/f86ae3c5bc792bee8d0e798c0af7e81b24f156572c02b10773e19258e9913134.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251038} {:answer/id #uuid "948ed4e4-d63f-5f9f-8126-d50ffaf910f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944026/assets/7547d4fa001c7bd0db9e6cd7751ba0da3cd4b65ef2fa4af6ea3c3fb80da55d8c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251039} {:answer/id #uuid "b448c9c5-0a5a-5dea-b6ab-2398a18830b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944026/assets/b6ebfd08f792396eaa6d1018690b7685616c26ec8ca2824f754da7ca19069108.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251040}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "948ed4e4-d63f-5f9f-8126-d50ffaf910f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944026/assets/7547d4fa001c7bd0db9e6cd7751ba0da3cd4b65ef2fa4af6ea3c3fb80da55d8c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251039} :answer-field/id #uuid "341eea2d-2df4-51ad-bb17-9b3734df9735" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251035}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d786a9f1-6d9d-573d-9964-69c5e58662eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-102107" :question/problem "Which of the following number lines gives the solution to $-9<6-5x<1?$" :question/worked-solution "We isolate $x$ by applying the addition and multiplication principles, as usual. \n\nFirst, we apply the addition principle:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-9 & <6-5x<1 \\\\ -9-6 & <6-5x-6<1-6 \\\\ -15 & <-5x<-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide by $-5.$ Note that since we are dividing by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality signs. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-15 & <-5x<-5 \\\\ \\frac{-15}{-5} & >\\frac{-5x}{-5}>\\frac{-5}{-5} \\\\ 3 & >x>1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution can be written as $3>x>1$, but this is somewhat difficult to read because the larger number is on the left rather than the right. So, we will rewrite the solution by reversing the order of the numbers: \n\n$$\n1<x<3\n$$\n\nWe can represent this solution using a number line, as follows.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944026/assets/7547d4fa001c7bd0db9e6cd7751ba0da3cd4b65ef2fa4af6ea3c3fb80da55d8c.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186251041 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5930113e-6971-59c9-810a-97fd25bc4f89" :knowledge-point/title "Compound Inequalities That Require Flipping the Inequality Sign"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16f8f0db-8372-5485-8269-b47a22d99fe7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251043}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16f8f0db-8372-5485-8269-b47a22d99fe7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251043} :answer-field/id #uuid "29e1aa8a-fe7f-58ea-80db-e3ab7f12076a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251042} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59fc50bc-a1e2-51ee-931a-ac12b4b28938" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251045}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "59fc50bc-a1e2-51ee-931a-ac12b4b28938" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251045} :answer-field/id #uuid "887c8d95-f786-5f8c-95b7-324009ffa8ec" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251044} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42864999-0200-54e2-b31c-ffc692e9f492" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251047}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42864999-0200-54e2-b31c-ffc692e9f492" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251047} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c758129-9679-5a97-b97c-305f35a1a710" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251046}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a9ab535b-0b78-5e31-996f-0a66ae30c4d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-214697" :question/problem "Find the solution to the inequality $-4\\le -3x-7<2.$\n\n$-3$\n{{field-1}}\n$x$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "We isolate $x$ by applying the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4 & \\le -3x-7<2 \\\\ -4+7 & \\le -3x-7+7<2+7 \\\\ 3 & \\le -3x<9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide by $-3.$ Note that since we are dividing by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality signs.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 & \\le -3x<9 \\\\ \\frac{3}{-3} & \\ge \\frac{-3x}{-3}>\\frac{9}{-3} \\\\ -1 & \\ge x>-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution can be written as $-1\\ge x>-3$, but this is somewhat difficult to read because the larger number is on the left rather than the right. So, we will rewrite the solution by reversing the order of the numbers: \n\n$$\n-3<x\\le -1\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186251048 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7229f1d0-4ba7-50ff-b5be-5697c886a175" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Compound Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a13015b8-0307-51b9-a439-4cbd957dc243" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251050}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a13015b8-0307-51b9-a439-4cbd957dc243" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251050} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ec2be3b-1ce5-5815-a35b-8bb48678c025" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251049} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3f9e5f8-2fee-5e48-8d31-5688c4211962" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251052}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3f9e5f8-2fee-5e48-8d31-5688c4211962" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251052} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd8fcef4-024c-59e3-b5db-e91e01352995" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251051} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc0e3cc5-5d44-55e6-be74-d29baeb46076" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251054}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc0e3cc5-5d44-55e6-be74-d29baeb46076" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251054} :answer-field/id #uuid "61da6a81-c97c-52dc-8b0b-0c97cba1ae90" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251053}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "032565a3-2a3d-5b47-9d7c-717280dce6e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-214698" :question/problem "Find the solution to the inequality $1<\\frac{x-2}{3}<2.$\n\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n$x$\n{{field-3}}\n$8$" :question/worked-solution "We isolate $x$ by applying the addition and multiplication principles, as usual.\n\nFirst, we multiply by $3$ to eliminate the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & <\\frac{x-2}{3}<2 \\\\ 3\\cdot 1 & <3\\cdot \\frac{x-2}{3}<3\\cdot 2 \\\\ 3 & <x-2<6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we continue isolating $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 & <x-2<6 \\\\ 3+2 & <x-2+2<6+2 \\\\ 5 & <x<8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $5<x<8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186251055 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7229f1d0-4ba7-50ff-b5be-5697c886a175" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Compound Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec9265a1-2bb6-56da-8347-fa8653fd6463" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251057}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec9265a1-2bb6-56da-8347-fa8653fd6463" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251057} :answer-field/id #uuid "01011713-b3a3-5d48-953d-510cfd579c44" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251056} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ae99fbe-43d7-52e2-ae8d-fbae65f70bc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251059}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ae99fbe-43d7-52e2-ae8d-fbae65f70bc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251059} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec4082ba-9a47-5027-bd6e-5dab4b4b1b54" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251058} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76ce2c85-ef2f-5539-8bef-cadd37a5dbdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251061}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76ce2c85-ef2f-5539-8bef-cadd37a5dbdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251061} :answer-field/id #uuid "c04b282b-7b43-5e42-bd69-bd896a101710" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251060}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c5f41c51-7776-5185-a86c-e8758c47b0c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-214755" :question/problem "Find the solution to the inequality $1<\\frac{x+5}{3}\\le 2.$\n\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}$\\,x\\le $\n\n{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "We isolate $x$ by applying the addition and multiplication principles, as usual.\n\nFirst, we multiply by $3$ to eliminate the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & <\\frac{x+5}{3}\\le 2 \\\\ 3\\cdot 1 & <3\\cdot \\frac{x+5}{3}\\le 3\\cdot 2 \\\\ 3 & <x+5\\le 6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we continue isolating $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 & <x+5\\le 6 \\\\ 3-5 & <x+5-5\\le 6-5 \\\\ -2 & <x\\le 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $-2<x\\le 1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186251062 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5930113e-6971-59c9-810a-97fd25bc4f89" :knowledge-point/title "Compound Inequalities That Require Flipping the Inequality Sign"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f219775d-8b9e-586d-9994-ccd551dd06cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251064} {:answer/id #uuid "87add3b4-b764-5fb8-8a02-2234b9be5731" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251065}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87add3b4-b764-5fb8-8a02-2234b9be5731" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251065} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2136416-78b8-5117-af7f-0d57873c940c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251063} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50e1f226-9ff0-52d9-98a2-7719f6cef0f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251067}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50e1f226-9ff0-52d9-98a2-7719f6cef0f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251067} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fb646f6-985a-5556-88fc-db1f42f3de77" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251066} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "069f8651-a51a-5f12-85ab-d7bf95badbba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251069}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "069f8651-a51a-5f12-85ab-d7bf95badbba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251069} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ee9f58c-7a3e-50dd-a9d0-0975cc13daf3" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251068}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6cb893b7-f26a-5b4b-a638-240ae0268c56" :question/math-academy-id "q-214796" :question/problem "Find the solution to the inequality $-2\\,<\\frac{6-2x}{\\,4}\\,\\le \\,4.$\n\n$-5$\n{{field-1}}\n$x$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "We isolate $x$ by applying the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2 & <\\frac{6-2x}{\\,4}\\le 4 \\\\ 4\\cdot (-2) & <4\\cdot \\frac{6-2x}{4}\\le 4\\cdot 4 \\\\ -8 & <6-2x\\le 16 \\\\ -8-6 & <6-2x-6\\le 16-6 \\\\ -14 & <-2x\\le 10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nAt this point, we need to divide by $-2.$ However, because we are dividing by a negative, we also need to flip the inequality signs.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-14 & <-2x\\le 10 \\\\ \\frac{-14}{-2} & >\\frac{-2x}{-2}\\ge \\frac{10}{-2} \\\\ 7 & >x\\ge -5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe solution can be written as $7>x\\ge -5,$ but this is somewhat difficult to read because the larger number is on the left rather than the right. So, we will rewrite the solution by reversing the order of the numbers:\n\n$$\n-5\\le x<7\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186251070 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5930113e-6971-59c9-810a-97fd25bc4f89" :knowledge-point/title "Compound Inequalities That Require Flipping the Inequality Sign"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c8f6f72-c57f-54b4-9757-4e3b5447b20c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251072} {:answer/id #uuid "905c3623-8175-51df-a9d8-99d5173355d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251073}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "905c3623-8175-51df-a9d8-99d5173355d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251073} :answer-field/id #uuid "19639fd3-f78d-509f-8e2b-7cde8fad1880" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251071} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1dfe27e-0e0e-58ea-ba1f-d24faa8e91d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251075}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1dfe27e-0e0e-58ea-ba1f-d24faa8e91d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251075} :answer-field/id #uuid "a1e4d685-39d9-5256-a78c-ea4b859b62c4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251074} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45d23258-0bc3-588f-8f62-7e0ccd1617e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251077}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45d23258-0bc3-588f-8f62-7e0ccd1617e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251077} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2b24b05-9e8b-5729-8908-61ac17a2bd7e" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251076}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9e765d30-ad54-5349-a2bd-4b92ac6cfd52" :question/math-academy-id "q-214799" :question/problem "Find the solution to the inequality $3<\\frac{3-6x}{7}<9.$\n\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n\n$x<$\n{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "We isolate $x$ by applying the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 & <\\frac{3-6x}{7}<9 \\\\ 7\\cdot 3 & <7\\cdot \\frac{3-6x}{7}<7\\cdot 9 \\\\ 21 & <3-6x<63 \\\\ 21-3 & <3-6x-3<63-3 \\\\ 18 & <-6x<60\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nAt this point, we need to divide by $-6.$ However, because we are dividing by a negative, we also need to flip the inequality signs.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}18 & <-6x<60 \\\\ \\frac{18}{-6} & >\\frac{-6x}{-6}>\\frac{60}{-6} \\\\ -3 & >x>-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe solution can be written as $-3>\\,x\\,>-10,$ but this is somewhat difficult to read because the larger number is on the left rather than the right. So, we will rewrite the solution by reversing the order of the numbers:\n\n$$\n-10<x<-3\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186251078 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5930113e-6971-59c9-810a-97fd25bc4f89" :knowledge-point/title "Compound Inequalities That Require Flipping the Inequality Sign"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82831d59-7e0c-5185-8100-b386e0f85d0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\le x<4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251080} {:answer/id #uuid "1949e5da-1261-5ed9-a1b2-a2b960547bd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2<x\\le 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251081} {:answer/id #uuid "e9b4a57f-354d-5667-9d63-75ade21c25e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4<x\\le -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251082} {:answer/id #uuid "5756c84a-86e3-55ab-8662-a8982c421da7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2<x\\le 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251083} {:answer/id #uuid "a0544622-0328-5a62-8ba5-e0f350ce2794" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\le x<-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251084}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82831d59-7e0c-5185-8100-b386e0f85d0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\le x<4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251080} :answer-field/id #uuid "820710b1-7f40-5f5c-b381-ba76cadedeb2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251079}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c3487c93-c625-5874-bcbd-3c8264cbcbc0" :question/math-academy-id "q-29046" :question/problem "What is the solution to $\\,-3<5-2x\\le 1?$" :question/worked-solution "We isolate $x$ by applying the addition and multiplication principles, as usual. \n\nFirst, we apply the addition principle:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3 & <5-2x\\le 1 \\\\ -3-5 & <5-2x-5\\le 1-5 \\\\ -8 & <-2x\\le -4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide by $-2.$ Note that since we are dividing by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality signs.\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-8 & <-2x\\le -4 \\\\ \\frac{-8}{-2} & >x\\ge \\frac{-4}{-2} \\\\ 4 & >x\\ge 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution can be written as $4>x\\ge 2$, but this is somewhat difficult to read because the larger number is on the left rather than the right. So, we will rewrite the solution by reversing the order of the numbers: $2\\le x<4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186251085 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7229f1d0-4ba7-50ff-b5be-5697c886a175" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Compound Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1bcaa14-e541-561b-a2e1-718107b7fee1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0<x<2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251087} {:answer/id #uuid "32468234-b7c5-5973-9b85-f80724dc8eae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2<x<2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251088} {:answer/id #uuid "000a5992-53fc-5cca-928c-a418770a99af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4<x<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251089} {:answer/id #uuid "0cc3a63b-baa8-5e5f-b731-fc491d6c923c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4<x<2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251090} {:answer/id #uuid "bfe09680-d535-5860-a6cb-731c2ef20ac0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2<x<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251091}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1bcaa14-e541-561b-a2e1-718107b7fee1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0<x<2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251087} :answer-field/id #uuid "39611264-f252-5003-87f5-bb72c0ddd129" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251086}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "41e69b26-46d4-5072-9c49-7f6166874f3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-29055" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $\\,-2<\\,2x-2\\,<2.$" :question/worked-solution "We isolate $x$ by applying the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2 & <\\,2x-2\\,<2 \\\\ -2+2 & <2x-2+2<2+2 \\\\ 0 & <2x<4 \\\\ \\frac{0}{2} & <\\frac{2x}{2}<\\frac{4}{2} \\\\ 0 & <x<2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $0<x<2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186251092 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7229f1d0-4ba7-50ff-b5be-5697c886a175" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Compound Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92c876c4-1aa3-57ec-8011-5446a8d45a70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1<x<\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251094} {:answer/id #uuid "1534e659-7d62-588f-82d0-64aedca58ad3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10<x<\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251095} {:answer/id #uuid "86339e15-f8c6-5b31-9392-5e3b9c70a4f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}<x<-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251096} {:answer/id #uuid "0c661258-e343-5caf-b404-4d88776ab4e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}<x<10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251097} {:answer/id #uuid "0ea8e6fc-1909-5701-bcb1-d05cdb0b8858" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1<x<\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251098}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ea8e6fc-1909-5701-bcb1-d05cdb0b8858" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1<x<\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251098} :answer-field/id #uuid "78ca0120-ba14-5160-92e4-065799b4bc58" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251093}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "24c30c42-4d03-5a02-a7b6-b011ed8ec16b" :question/math-academy-id "q-3068" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $-1<\\frac{6x-8}{2}<1.$" :question/worked-solution "We isolate $x$ by applying the addition and multiplication principles, as usual.\n\nFirst, we multiply by $2$ to eliminate the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & <\\frac{6x-8}{2}<1 \\\\ -1\\cdot 2 & <\\frac{6x-8}{2}\\cdot 2<1\\cdot 2 \\\\ -2 & <6x-8<2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we continue isolating $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2 & <6x-8<2 \\\\ -2+8 & <6x-8+8<2+8 \\\\ 6 & <6x<10 \\\\ \\frac{6}{6} & <\\frac{6x}{6}<\\frac{10}{6} \\\\ 1 & <x<\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $1<x<\\frac{5}{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186251099 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b3ff37f0-6e45-5da4-ac87-1b93c8df3e80" :knowledge-point/title "Representing Solutions of Compound Inequalities on Number Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc553201-a411-5f67-8861-c683a5f2f038" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944026/assets/1a3b83780bbd15328077dc45eef965aaf311e704990ee3cb45078d76c96183a2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251101} {:answer/id #uuid "b93f0424-2b51-5ec7-932b-8875a323de40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944026/assets/c8c019b0d7a2b34e9791394ce1ac50f8db22b1d7fb9296a8c119a80a583d63ef.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251102} {:answer/id #uuid "f6db15fc-3e23-5809-bfa3-3369b96d5a5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944026/assets/91ec8574742229a2c7fd5af8920f9137e2b25e28a6f02a7cf1edcc8a4db4b6d5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251103} {:answer/id #uuid "9c79d8c5-7efe-5a80-81df-6f8840c07d58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944026/assets/d3ff8ace8f19f48631b57968c7aad223613e65f5be6f67a3196bd5fa9158ae51.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251104} {:answer/id #uuid "0c49631d-2f68-52c2-bd45-e873bb1c10d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944026/assets/5a8e25a0a97ec193574fd8099e2dfdce70ed887e9f527b855b1ca0957ae7885b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251105}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6db15fc-3e23-5809-bfa3-3369b96d5a5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944026/assets/91ec8574742229a2c7fd5af8920f9137e2b25e28a6f02a7cf1edcc8a4db4b6d5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251103} :answer-field/id #uuid "748d7566-8b33-5499-a243-59208ab01908" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251100}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e996239f-cafe-55a4-9e1e-af5edfdca48f" :question/math-academy-id "q-44761" :question/problem "Which of the following number lines gives the solution to $-1<-5x-6<4?$" :question/worked-solution "We isolate $x$ by applying the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & <-5x-6<4 \\\\ -1+6 & <-5x-6+6<4+6 \\\\ 5 & <-5x<10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt this point, we need to divide by $-5.$ However, because we are dividing by a negative, we also need to flip the signs of the inequalities.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & <-5x<10 \\\\ \\frac{5}{-5} & >\\frac{-5x}{-5}>\\frac{10}{-5} \\\\ -1 & >x>-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution can be written as $-1>x>-2$, but this is somewhat difficult to read because the larger number is on the left rather than the right. So, we will rewrite the solution by reversing the order of the numbers: \n\n$$\n-2<x<-1\n$$\n\nWe can represent this solution using a number line, as follows.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944026/assets/91ec8574742229a2c7fd5af8920f9137e2b25e28a6f02a7cf1edcc8a4db4b6d5.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186251106 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b3ff37f0-6e45-5da4-ac87-1b93c8df3e80" :knowledge-point/title "Representing Solutions of Compound Inequalities on Number Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "201f091f-0165-5691-9ebe-a9fae58bdd35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944026/assets/bab168cd93d52c9a36f8d5bc8e905f009b2779618643acafaa4fae7eeb28abca.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251108} {:answer/id #uuid "c020dc9b-5418-5e36-8b46-35360e77fb3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944026/assets/125b76bf34776d2512d42d8528d3b295111ff6ca505ea4aada4b7aabcbd8a713.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251109} {:answer/id #uuid "487d41e0-87ec-50b0-8860-e039ed3a02c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944026/assets/